{"id":"a0906e5184364ca3afecef163d25bb84","owner":"FairfaxCounty","ownerId":"b9173013540c15a75aec878ffd638370","orgId":"ioennV6PpG5Xodq0","created":1602689199000,"modified":1727438382000,"guid":null,"name":"Sewer_Service_Areas","title":"Sewer Service Areas - Interim Layer","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span><span>The delineation of the ASSA boundary is to include the immediately adjacent area which can be served by the smallest allowable publicly owned gravity lines installed in accord with normal engineering practices which will result in the safest and most cost-effective operation. Any extension of a public sewer line across the surface drainage divide of the ASSA shall not exceed a distance of 400 feet nor a manhole depth of 12 feet without the approval of the Board of Supervisors. <\/span><\/span><span><span>The ASSA feature layer has a field name SERVICE that has three options:<\/span><\/span><\/p><ul><li><p style='margin:3 0 0 0;'><span><span>INSIDE ASSA - these are areas within the ASSA boundary<\/span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p style='margin:3 0 0 0;'><span><span>OUTSIDE ASSA - areas that are outside of the ASSA boundary and cannot receive sewer service<\/span><\/span><\/p><\/li><li><p style='margin:0 0 11 0;'><span><span>BY OTHERS \u2013 areas of sewer service that are served by other jurisdictions<\/span><\/span><\/p><\/li><\/ul><div><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>Questions regarding this data layer should be directed to the <\/span><a href='https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/contact/MailForm.aspx?agId=35' style='color:rgb(0, 97, 155); text-decoration-line:none; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Department of Planning and Development.<\/a><br /><\/div><p><span><span><\/span><\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["Fairfax County","Virginia","GIS","FFX","DPWES","DPWES GIS Services","BPS","BSS","WWM","WPMD","WCD","Sanitary Sewer","Approved Sewer Service Area","ASSA","VA"],"snippet":"This data set contains areas of approved sewer service within the County. This delineation of the sewer service area boundary is used to decide whether the...","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail1603222054830.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-77.5400104710668,38.61543309058031],[-77.0347932426929,39.059547087160794]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102746","accessInformation":"Fairfax County, Virginia; DPWES GIS Services; Wastewater Management","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><p style='margin:0 0 11 0;'><span style='font-size:12pt; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; background-image:initial; background-position:initial; background-size:initial; background-repeat:initial; background-attachment:initial; background-origin:initial; background-clip:initial;'>Please review the <\/span><span style='font-size:12pt; font-family:Arial, sans-serif;'><a href='https://www.fairfaxcounty.gov/maps/disclaimer' style='color:rgb(0, 97, 155); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); background-image:initial; background-position:initial; background-size:initial; background-repeat:initial; background-attachment:initial; background-origin:initial; background-clip:initial;'>Fairfax County GIS Division disclaimer<\/span><\/a><\/span><br /><\/p><div><div><p><span><\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/ioennV6PpG5Xodq0/arcgis/rest/services/Sewer_Service_Areas/FeatureServ